WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, everybody.
Welcome to "Corrections"

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the week of Monday,
June 24th.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is going to be our last
"Corrections" for a bit.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.146
We're about to go on a two-wee
hiatus, which is very exciting

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone here
has different plans.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:19.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to
a reeducation camp...

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:25.158
...where I'm going to lear
how to say "substantive"

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:28.094 line:92%
without double clutching.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's get started.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking about
the cyber ninjas

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were involved
in the Arizona election audit.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:38.505 size:75% position:38%
We said cyber ninjas
sounded like a game

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would find
in the bargain bin at GameStop

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.510 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in 1994.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.812 line:92%
GameStop wasn't around in 1994

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was told
by quite a few people.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
We should have said Babbage'
or FuncoLand.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:55.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, I said it wrong.
It's GameStops.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:01.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we have a lot
of international viewers

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
that engage with the show
on YouTube.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
We feel very grateful
to have them.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of British people told m
I said "buoy" wrong.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was incorrect.
I said it right.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:18.578 line:92%
But it turns out, in England

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.881 size:88% position:44% line:92%
they pronounce it "boy,"

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is bad.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.685 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How will we know
where our lobster trap is?

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.691 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"We'll tie it to a boy."

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The boy will float
in the water,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's how we will kno
where our trap is.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.268 line:92%
And when it is time to sup

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.872 line:92%
we will return to the boy

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.006 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to capture our prey."

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And will we bring the boy
back with us?"

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.278 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"The boy will stay."

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that's interesting.
It's boy.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:58.218 size:75% position:38%
It's boy in England.
It's "booey" here.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.420 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And then, in Scotland,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
according to our photographe
Lloyd, it's "bay!"

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, I take it
with a grain --

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
a grain of salt
when it comes from old Lloyd

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.034 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got in a little
back and forth, you and I,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is...

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said that we beep
our curse words,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you said the correct ter
is bleep our curse words,

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.887 size:81% position:41%
and I basically said
it -- it's immaterial.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.755 line:92%
It doesn't make a difference

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
People pointed out
on the actual --

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:42.228 size:78% position:39%
our closed captioning
that we put on this,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
we say bleep.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.231 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So I was 100% wrong.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:49.502
And again, I would have know
that if I ever watched this,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but why would I?

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:55.808 size:84% position:42%
Why would I reengage
with this whole charade

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.444 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a second time?

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, last week
in "Corrections,"

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said the sentence
"You the audience is relieved.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
A bunch of you -- It was the
biggest correction of the week
--

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.026 line:92%
said that my grammar was wrong

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:18.364
and I should have said,
"You the audience are relieved."

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.199 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is correct,

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:24.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's also a reminder
that you the audience

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
both is and are

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
[Seth yells "beep"]
insufferable.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh. We talked about

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:38.418 size:78% position:39%
the Phil Collins song
"In the Air Tonight"

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
and talked about the drum solo
in that song.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of our viewers
reached out and said

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:48.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's technically not
a drum solo, it's a drum fill.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.063 line:92%
And I don't want to stereotype

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm going to go
out on a limb and say

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the person who wrote that
is a stepdad.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:59.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, I heard you guys talking
from the other room."

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.843
"Ugh, not now, Dave."
"No, I just want to let you know

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:07.347
a little something about, uh
the song you're talking about.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.881 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"We don't care, Dave."

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, uh, I just --
It matters.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It matters, guys.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.022 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a drum fill.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:20.760
And one day, you're going
to be in Guitar Center,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're going to
embarrass yourself.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.531 line:92%
I'm trying to help you out."

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.833 line:92%
"Just get out of here, Dave.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.501 line:92%
"Alright, I'm going to go.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.005 size:78% position:39%
Also, you guys should
listen to Genesis.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.474 line:92%
I mean, that's the real stuff.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Selling England By the Pound,
that's -- The prog stuff.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.416 size:88% position:44%
You know, I mean, 'cause
God bless later Collins,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.984 line:92%
but it's a little pop radio.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:48.354 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Get out of here, Dave!"

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.455 line:92%
"Also, it's an urban legend.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you
talking about, Dave?"

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:54.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Uh, y-you know, that that's
about someone drowning."

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:57.630
"What -- I don't even know
what you're talking about.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"It's not real.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's just not real.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.203 line:92%
They thought it was a boy,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:07.073 line:92%
but then they got closer,

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:09.475 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and it was just a boy."

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:09.942 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"What?"

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They thought
it was a boy drowning.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it was a boy."

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't --
What are you talking about

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, uh, well, Col--
Phil Collins is British,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:24.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I was using the British
pronunciation of buoy."

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.765 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We talked about Sal...

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.435 line:92%
[Seth yells "beep"] up real bad.

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:36.869 line:92%
He was talking about coffee,

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he talked about the
difference between a coffee --

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:40.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a cappuccino
and a latte.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:44.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I said that Sal's
not really a fancy coffee guy,

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.345 line:92%
and we should have known better.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said that he --
he, like, fries Sanka a pan,

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:53.052 size:78% position:39%
and then he drains it
through a Mets cap.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:57.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was that sentence
I was then told,

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.658 size:75% position:38% line:92%
you can't fry water.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:03.396
Sanka's instant coffee,
so you wouldn't need to do that,

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:07.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you don't drain it,
you strain it.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:10.203 line:92%
So that's -- that's a hat trick.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very hard to pull off on -
on television in the modern ag

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:20.980 size:84% position:42%
to make three mistakes
in one sentence, but...

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
your boy did it.

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also stumbled,
because I was doing --

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Chuckles ]
I was talking about the fact

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
if Dennis Miller had been aske

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Sal
and his knowledge of coffee,

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:42.535
Dennis Miller would have said...
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:47.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sal thinks macchiato's
the new Latin dance craze,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.276 line:92%
courtesy of Los Del Rio."

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.981 line:92%
And then a bunch of people said,

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:59.452
"Your Dennis Miller sounds like,
'A,' Mike Lindell,

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:03.089 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
'B,' Paul Lynde."

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which immediately gave me
an idea for a new character.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Paul Lyndell...

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:19.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
...who would be
the center square, you know --

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tic Tac Toe?
Was that the name of the show?

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:25.511 size:78% position:39%
-"Hollywood Squares."
-"Hollywood Squares."

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:28.314 line:92%
So you'd have Paul Lyndell

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:30.283 line:92%
You know, the host would say

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:33.219 line:92%
"According to Reader's Digest,

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:37.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
what's the worst thing
a man can come home

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.625 line:92%
and find his wife doing?"

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:44.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it would cut to, uh
you know, Paul Lyndell,

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.233 line:92%
and he's say "Hugo Chavez!

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:48.801 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Snickering laugh ]

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:58.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to try to re-auditio
for "SNL."

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:05.418 size:78% position:39%
I said "Appalaychan."
It's "Appalatchan."

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I called NFL player Carl
"Naseeb" -- It's Carl Nassib

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said --
This, twice this week.

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:19.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steven Seagal,
I called him Steven "Saygal.

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that one's a bummer,
because I realize

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:27.507
I've seen more Steven Seagal
movies than Clark Gable movies

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:31.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't call him
Clork Gerbel.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.912
And, you know, that guy's
going through a tough time

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:36.382 size:78% position:39%
Steven Seagal's going
through a tough time.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.550 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I said it right, right?

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause, you know, he's, like
friends with Putin now,

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:42.188
and, you know, he kind of gets
dragged in the press right -

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:43.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Guy's under siege.

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:46.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- Look, and again --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can criticize him
for what he does.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:50.296 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He's not above the law.

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, he shouldn'
be marked for death.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I, you know,
this is my show,

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're making
an executive decision

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:58.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
not to make fun
of the guy anymore,

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:00.740 line:92%
'cause I'm not out for justice

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.009 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:05.211 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's not me.

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have a light.

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:09.982 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm a glimmer man.

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:17.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ooh, I talked about
my Pixar movie,

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:19.792 line:92%
and I have very good updates

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:24.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
on my World War II
Pixar movie about

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:27.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
American chickens
who go undercover in Germany

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.869
But -- And again, this goes back
to the benefits

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:33.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
of having international
viewership --

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:35.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
Germans said, "Hey,
right off the bat,

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Germans would know
these are American chickens,

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:43.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Germany, they do not
sell eggs by the dozen.

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
10 at a time.

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:48.087
And I was going to call it "Th
Dirty Dozen," so that's out.

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:52.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now it's either
"The Great Eggscape"

00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:54.727 line:92%
or "Force Hen from Navarone.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.597 --> 00:10:01.834
I also talked about the fact
that it -- Again, go back.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to re-explain
the plot to you.

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:07.740 size:84% position:42%
Just go back and watch
the last "Corrections."

00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:10.276 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:12.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay. So, I talked about
how at the very end,

00:10:12.845 --> 00:10:18.317
before the German captain cuts
off the head of the rooster,

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:20.753 size:78% position:39%
the American rooster,
who has outed himself

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:27.026
by saying cock-a-doodle-do
instead of kee-kee-ree-kee -

00:10:27.026 --> 00:10:29.495 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, the German captain,

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:31.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
right before he cuts off
the rooster's head,

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
the rooster winks
to his -- his companions.

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:41.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, roosters can't wink,
I was told.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.745
They have -- They have a top
and a bottom eyelid that close

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:49.248 line:92%
but only when they sleep.

00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:53.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have a third
translucent eyelid.

00:10:53.552 --> 00:10:57.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like a --
It's a nictitating membran

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that wipes --

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wipes the -- the eye
when it needs it.

00:11:02.128 --> 00:11:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's, like,
an interesting fact

00:11:03.963 --> 00:11:08.534
if you're ever trying to..
clear out a dinner party.

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.504 --> 00:11:13.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now I can't -- I have
this really emotional moment

00:11:13.673 --> 00:11:15.741
at the end of the film where
you know, the rooster winks,

00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:19.178
and now I know
that roosters can't wink, and...

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:23.582
so I have to come up with
a different ending for the film.

00:11:23.582 --> 00:11:26.752 line:92%
So, I never said what animal

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:29.488 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the German captain was.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a walrus.

00:11:31.457 --> 00:11:35.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think originally
when I pitched it,

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:38.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
people had kind of hoped
it would be another farm anima

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:42.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
just for consistency.
But I said, well, the thing is

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
walruses are, like, an anima
with a mustache.

00:11:45.004 --> 00:11:47.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think it'd be really fun
for the kids

00:11:47.306 --> 00:11:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see a walrus
with a Hitler mustache.

00:11:51.744 --> 00:11:53.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:54.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you know,
the Pixar people,

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:59.318
they mocked it up and said
"Well, something like this?"

00:11:59.318 --> 00:12:01.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:04.824 size:88% position:44%
And then, like, you know
how they've been doing,

00:12:04.824 --> 00:12:06.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a lot of
live-action stuff,

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:08.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a live-action
"Jungle Book,"

00:12:08.427 --> 00:12:11.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, a live-action
"Lion King"?

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:12.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
They would do it
with the walrus,

00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:16.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it would
look like this.

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:17.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Chuckles ]

00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:20.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:24.844 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Anyway, the walrus...

00:12:24.844 --> 00:12:26.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
was going to cut off
the head of --

00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:28.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, I should also mention
the character's name

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:30.416 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is Christoph Waltzrus.

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:32.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:32.818 --> 00:12:37.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, Christoph Waltzru
says to the rooster,

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:41.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's like,
"I will see you in hell!"

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:44.029 line:92%
and then cuts off his head

00:12:44.029 --> 00:12:46.031 line:92%
And then he turns to the hen

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are on a hill
in Allied territory,

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:51.504
and he goes, "And I will fin
each and every one of you!

00:12:51.504 --> 00:12:52.505 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I will chase you down!"

00:12:52.505 --> 00:12:53.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's giving
this real speech,

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:57.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's a -- it's a tight sho
of this walrus, right?

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:58.277 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And then he's talking --

00:12:58.277 --> 00:13:00.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's like this, you know?
He's talking to the hens,

00:13:00.379 --> 00:13:01.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's like,
"I will find you!"

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:03.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then all of a sudden,
he just stops,

00:13:03.115 --> 00:13:03.849 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and he's like [Gurgles]

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:06.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know that thing in movie
where, like, people die

00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:07.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, blood
starts immediately

00:13:07.419 --> 00:13:09.188
coming out of their mouth
and it's like [Gurgles]

00:13:09.188 --> 00:13:14.360
then the walrus' head
just, like, slides off its body.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.995 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And you see behind it

00:13:15.995 --> 00:13:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the rooster
whose head has been cut off,

00:13:19.365 --> 00:13:24.970
using the chicken's magic powe
of being able to run around,

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.873 size:78% position:39% line:92%
has picked up the ax,

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:29.608 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and its headless body

00:13:29.608 --> 00:13:31.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
has cut off the head
of the walrus.

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:34.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, anyway,
I think it'll be fun for kids.

00:13:34.814 --> 00:13:37.883 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:40.753
Lastly -- Were a lot of --
In "Corrections" this week

00:13:40.753 --> 00:13:42.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
there were a lot
of Corrections people

00:13:42.454 --> 00:13:44.757 line:92%
correcting the correctors,

00:13:44.757 --> 00:13:45.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, saying
that Baze was right.

00:13:45.758 --> 00:13:48.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, there are cheat code
in "Metal Gear Solid."

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:52.331
Some people were even backing up
Sal on his coffee stuff.

00:13:52.331 --> 00:13:53.299 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And another one was,

00:13:53.299 --> 00:13:56.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
we mentioned
Finland having mountains.

00:13:56.235 --> 00:13:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
People said there are
no mountains in Finland.

00:13:57.937 --> 00:13:59.638 size:84% position:42%
We corrected ourselves,
and then people said

00:13:59.638 --> 00:14:02.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
there actually are
some mountains in Finland.

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:03.609 line:92%
And -- And nothing's worse

00:14:03.609 --> 00:14:05.377 size:78% position:39%
than when the jackals
attack the jackals.

00:14:05.377 --> 00:14:08.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
So just try to find
common ground, guys.

00:14:08.681 --> 00:14:12.017
It's you against me.
It's not you against each other.

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:15.454
But there is -- There are
some Finnish mountains.

00:14:15.454 --> 00:14:18.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this was a very
interesting story.

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:19.425 line:92%
There's one called Halti.

00:14:19.425 --> 00:14:20.926 line:92%
Hope I'm saying that right

00:14:20.926 --> 00:14:23.362 line:92%
I mean, I don't really...

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:24.563 size:81% position:41% line:92%
care that much, but...

00:14:24.563 --> 00:14:27.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
Halti is on the
Norwegian-Finnish border.

00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:30.903 size:78% position:39%
And a few years ago,
the people of Norway,

00:14:30.903 --> 00:14:34.273 size:88% position:44%
some people said, "Hey,
for Finland's centenary,

00:14:34.273 --> 00:14:36.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're going to move our border
200 meters,

00:14:36.242 --> 00:14:39.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then the entire mountain
will belong to Finland,"

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
which seems like --
And what a nice gift.

00:14:41.914 --> 00:14:45.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they
changed their mind.

00:14:45.117 --> 00:14:49.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, I know somebody
like that in my life,

00:14:49.622 --> 00:14:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
who -- who is like that
with gifts.

00:14:52.992 --> 00:14:56.095 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's Mikey the Shoe,

00:14:56.095 --> 00:14:58.297 line:92%
who's a terrible gift giver.

00:14:58.297 --> 00:15:01.967 line:92%
A few years ago for Christmas,

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:06.805
you know,
we give each other gifts, and...

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:09.008 line:92%
I got him a beautiful gift

00:15:09.008 --> 00:15:10.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Beautiful gold --

00:15:10.943 --> 00:15:15.447 line:92%
a goblet engraved with his name.

00:15:15.447 --> 00:15:17.049 line:92%
And then he came into my room,

00:15:17.049 --> 00:15:21.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he gave me a pair
of, like, um,

00:15:21.954 --> 00:15:24.223 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
fingerless gloves,

00:15:24.223 --> 00:15:26.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
just, like, ratty,

00:15:26.492 --> 00:15:28.260 size:88% position:44% line:92%
brown fingerless gloves.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"Oh, do you like it?"

00:15:30.195 --> 00:15:32.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "No,
I don't like it at all."

00:15:32.298 --> 00:15:33.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes,
"Why don't you like it?"

00:15:33.165 --> 00:15:35.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "I just don't like
fingerless gloves."

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then -- And again,
shame on me, right?

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:44.810 size:88% position:44%
Like, everything he does
is leading to upset me.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.012
And instead, I just go, "I don't
like fingerless gloves,"

00:15:47.012 --> 00:15:48.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then what do you
think he does?

00:15:48.047 --> 00:15:52.384
He goes, "Well, I got you
a couple of fingers, too!"

00:15:52.384 --> 00:15:54.186 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
For Christmas.

00:15:54.186 --> 00:15:55.754 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:15:55.754 --> 00:16:00.025 line:92%
Well [Chuckles] two-week hiatus.

00:16:00.025 --> 00:16:02.027 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We love you all dearly.

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:04.063 line:92%
We do enjoy this time together

00:16:04.063 --> 00:16:08.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And we will see you
in July.

00:16:08.634 --> 00:16:10.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Stay safe, friends.

